Hi,
I've recently been working a bit on bringing SERefPoliy to Debian.
See also http://selinux.alioth.debian.org/experimental/
and the SELinux on Debian mailing lists.

Attached is a diff for the reference policy to add dpkg/apt-get
policies.
Note that this might break apt-get on Redhat, since I have no idea about
that interaction... But having /usr/bin/apt-get labeled rpm_exec_t
sounds weird to me anyway. ;-)

Also: is there a way to make the sendmail and postfix modules conflict?
They seem to interfere rather badly.

The dpkg policy doesn't use dpkg_script_t yet properly. When extracting
a new package, the new packages' scripts are not labeled correctly. I
guess a dpkg patch is required to fix that. But basic package
installation and removal hopefully should be okay now. Anyway, it's a
start... ;-)

No way to run refpolicy on Debian in full enforcing mode yet, though.

best regards,
Erich Schubert
